  "notes": "USAGE:\n- {体|からだ}を{鍛錬|たんれん}する (to train one's body)\n- {精神|せいしん}の{鍛錬|たんれん} (mental discipline)\n- {日々|ひび}の{鍛錬|たんれん} (daily training)\nImplies serious, rigorous training with the goal of strengthening or perfecting. Often used in martial arts, sports, and personal development contexts.\n\nETYMOLOGY:\nOriginally referred to forging metal (tempering). The meaning extended to forging/tempering the body and mind.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {訓練|くんれん} (training, drill - more general)\n- {修練|しゅうれん} (training, discipline - similar)\n- {鍛|きた}える (to forge, to train - verb)",
